{
  "id": "antigravity",
  "label": "Antigravity IDE + CLI (user profile)",
  "tool": "antigravity",
  "scope": "user",
  "requires_admin": false,
  "selectors": [
    "antigravity",
    "ag"
  ],
  "enforcement": {
    "windows": "advisory",
    "linux": "advisory",
    "darwin": "advisory"
  },
  "$comment": [
    "ONLY tool of the three without an admin layer. There is no equivalent of managed-settings",
    "(Claude) or requirements.toml (Codex): everything lives in the user profile and the",
    "developer can edit everything. 'advisory' across ALL THREE platforms, including Windows --",
    "the exception to the rollout rule.",
    "",
    "Rule precedence is DENY > ASK > ALLOW, by bucket and not by",
    "specificity. Practical consequence dictating the list below: a",
    "command(*) in ask would override all of allow. Therefore ask lists commands individually",
    "instead of using wildcards, and docker ps/images is NOT in",
    "allow -- command(docker) in ask would override it anyway. Same divergence",
    "accepted in Codex, for the same reason.",
    "",
    "This target inherited context files from gemini-user, removed when",
    "Gemini CLI was removed from the package: Antigravity reads ~/.gemini/GEMINI.md and the",
    "playbook beside it, so removing the Gemini target would have removed the Rules delivery",
    "for the tool that remains. The constant boundary applies: never write",
    "~/.gemini/settings.json, which is not ours."
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${HOME}/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json",
        "linux": "${HOME}/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json",
        "darwin": "${HOME}/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json"
      },
      "format": "json",
      "strategy": "merge-permission-lists",
      "list_parent": "permissions",
      "lists": [
        "deny",
        "ask",
        "allow"
      ],
      "payload": {
        "permissions": {
          "deny": [
            "read_file(.env)",
            "read_file(.env.local)",
            "read_file(secrets)",
            "read_file(credentials)",
            "read_file(id_rsa)",
            "read_file(id_ed25519)",
            "read_file(~/.ssh)",
            "read_file(~/.aws)",
            "read_file(~/.azure)",
            "read_file(~/.gnupg)",
            "read_file(~/.kube)",
            "read_file(~/.config/gcloud)",
            "read_file(~/.docker/config.json)",
            "read_file(~/.git-credentials)",
            "read_file(~/.netrc)",
            "read_file(~/.npmrc)",
            "read_file(~/.pypirc)",
            "read_file(~/.terraform.d/credentials.tfrc.json)",
            "write_file(~/.ssh)",
            "write_file(.git/)",
            "command(curl)",
            "command(wget)",
            "command(sudo)",
            "command(chmod 777)",
            "command(npm install -g)",
            "command(pip install)",
            "command(git push --force)",
            "command(git commit --no-verify)",
            "command(git config --global core.hooksPath)",
            "command(kubectl get secret)",
            "command(kubectl get secrets)",
            "command(kubectl describe secret)",
            "command(kubectl describe secrets)",
            "command(kubectl create token)",
            "execute_url(*)",
            "unsandboxed(*)",
            "command(git push -f)",
            "command(git filter-branch)"
          ],
          "ask": [
            "command(python)",
            "command(python3)",
            "command(node)",
            "command(npx)",
            "command(npm install)",
            "command(npm update)",
            "command(pnpm)",
            "command(yarn)",
            "command(bun)",
            "command(pipx)",
            "command(poetry)",
            "command(uv)",
            "command(docker)",
            "command(terraform apply)",
            "command(terraform plan)",
            "command(terraform show)",
            "command(terraform output)",
            "command(kubectl)",
            "command(git push)",
            "command(git commit)",
            "command(git clone)",
            "command(git config --global)",
            "command(git submodule update)",
            "command(git reset --hard)",
            "command(git clean)",
            "command(git rebase)",
            "command(git restore)",
            "command(git branch -D)",
            "command(git branch -d)",
            "command(git tag -d)",
            "command(git remote add)",
            "command(git remote set-url)",
            "command(git remote remove)",
            "command(git stash drop)",
            "command(git stash clear)"
          ],
          "allow": [
            "command(git status)",
            "command(git diff)",
            "command(git log)",
            "command(git add)",
            "command(git branch)",
            "command(npm run)",
            "command(npm test)",
            "command(semgrep)",
            "command(trivy)",
            "command(gitleaks)",
            "mcp(semgrep/*)",
            "command(git show)",
            "command(git fetch)",
            "command(git stash list)",
            "command(git blame)"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${HOME}/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json",
        "linux": "${HOME}/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json",
        "darwin": "${HOME}/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json"
      },
      "format": "json",
      "strategy": "merge-missing-keys",
      "$comment": "Secure defaults without overriding explicit developer choices: commands run in the sandbox and files outside the workspace remain unavailable. Antigravity has no admin layer; this is an advisory baseline, reassessed via reapply/audit.",
      "payload": {
        "toolPermission": "proceed-in-sandbox",
        "enableTerminalSandbox": true,
        "allowNonWorkspaceAccess": false
      }
    },
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${HOME}/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json",
        "linux": "${HOME}/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json",
        "darwin": "${HOME}/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json"
      },
      "format": "json",
      "strategy": "merge-mcp",
      "mcp_key": "mcpServers",
      "payload": {
        "mcpServers": {
          "semgrep": {
            "command": "semgrep",
            "args": [
              "mcp"
            ],
            "env": {
              "SEMGREP_RULES": "p/default"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${HOME}/.gemini/security-review-playbook.md",
        "linux": "${HOME}/.gemini/security-review-playbook.md",
        "darwin": "${HOME}/.gemini/security-review-playbook.md"
      },
      "format": "markdown",
      "strategy": "overwrite",
      "backup": true,
      "$comment": "Deep reference read ON-DEMAND -- not part of context files. core-guidelines points to it via relative name. overwrite instead of md-block: the entire file is ours, nothing for the developer to customize here.",
      "payload_file": "policy/security-review-playbook.md"
    },
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${HOME}/.gemini/brand-identity.md",
        "linux": "${HOME}/.gemini/brand-identity.md",
        "darwin": "${HOME}/.gemini/brand-identity.md"
      },
      "format": "markdown",
      "strategy": "overwrite",
      "$comment": "Group palette. On-demand, like the playbook: color matters only in front-end, documentation, or diagrams, avoiding prompt preamble bloat across the four tools.",
      "payload_file": "policy/brand-identity.md"
    },
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${HOME}/.gemini/GEMINI.md",
        "linux": "${HOME}/.gemini/GEMINI.md",
        "darwin": "${HOME}/.gemini/GEMINI.md"
      },
      "format": "markdown",
      "strategy": "md-block",
      "marker": "<!-- security-team-block -->",
      "compose": [
        "policy/core-runtime.md",
        "policy/vendor-antigravity.md"
      ],
      "$comment": "Antigravity reads AGENTS.md and GEMINI.md, and has no documented global path of its own -- guidelines arrive via this file, shared with Gemini CLI. md-block instead of overwrite because the developer writes here: in Gemini CLI /memory add wrote to this file, and that habit persists."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Current documentation confirms that read_file(.env) is relative to the workspace root and directories are recursive. No filename glob exists: the rule protects root .env/.env.local, not arbitrary nested .env files. Keep secrets outside the workspace; sandbox and allowNonWorkspaceAccess=false provide the containment boundary.",
    "Context is hierarchical and concatenated: ~/.gemini/GEMINI.md (global) + repo GEMINI.md + per directory. The file closest to cwd comes later and wins in conflicts, so global guidelines act as defaults, not hard ceilings."
  ]
}
